    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey so i had the flu like 3 weeks ago and finally felt better but now i'm feeling super weird. like i'm just completely wiped out and get really winded just walking up a few stairs. also my heart feels like it's fluttering or racing sometimes and there's this heavy feeling in my chest when i move around. is this just like long term fatigue from being sick or should i be worried?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your symptoms could be related to lingering fatigue after the flu, but it's also possible that you may be experiencing lingering effects of myocarditis, an inflammation of the heart muscle that can occur after the flu or other viral infections. The fluttering heart sensation and heavy chest feeling could indicate that your heart is working harder than normal, which may also be a sign of myocarditis. It's recommended that you consult with a doctor to rule out any potential complications.",
